WEBVTT

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:48.500
Mission time.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:50.630
We received a tip.

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:52.690
In the southern province of Nigel,

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:56.920
the civilians aren't receiving the supplies coming from Central.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:01:59.470
Go investigate the situation.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.000
From an anonymous, eh?

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.600
I don't like the feeling of this.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.780
This is also part of our job.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:10.290
Isn't this just another phony?

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:15.950
We got several tips similar
to this one before you joined, Corporal.

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:19.560
We went out to investigate on anonymous tips
and found out them to be false.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:23.780
Just a way for those that hate
the higher-ups to vent their anger.

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:27.090
They weren't all bogus, right?

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:29.060
Some were true, at least?

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:30.420
Sometimes.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.220
The majority of them were bogus, though.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:37.070
This had to happen when the LT's not here, right?

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:38.970
Stop complaining.

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:42.590
You'll be in charge of this investigation.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:43.840
Got it?

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:45.670
Me?

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:51.590
Well, I guess there's no other choice with the people we have right now.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:53.310
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:58.830
So, how about we bet on whether this one's bogus or not?

00:02:58.830 --> 00:02:59.360
I refuse.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:01.860
You're forgetting Mer-kun!

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.830
Mer-kun!

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:09.560
Are you still angry about the fact you got demoted?

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:14.130
Hey, did you hear the reason why the LT asked for a vacation?

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.630
Oh, about that...

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:22.180
I just happened to overhear this,

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:24.920
but apparently, she's going to see her fiancé.

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:28.200
Fiancé?!

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:29.950
You're kidding me...

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:42.780
Alice!

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:44.530
Are you done changing?

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.440
Yes, right away.

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:58.710
Hurry, hurry!

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:01.490
How long do you plan on making Schultz wait?

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:05.590
We are deeply sorry, Lord Schultz.

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:08.290
Alice will be down very soon.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:11.370
Not a problem at all, oneesama.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:15.090
I shall wait, no matter how many minutes... how many hours!

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:20.150
Sorry for the wait, Sister.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.610
You foolish girl!

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:30.040
Wh-What are you doing, Sister?

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:30.980
Quiet!

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:32.820
Is that how a maiden dresses?!

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:35.290
My, Elice-chan, don't do something that scary.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:36.170
Neesan...

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:40.400
What are you going to do
if you leave a mark on Alice's cute face?

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:42.180
It's good medicine for her.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:43.060
Sister!

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:45.590
This formal army attire is very honorable.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:47.700
And you think you can conquer men looking like that?

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.850
Th-That was never part of my plans at all.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.580
Do you understand what's going on?

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:56.320
"He" will be escorting you at tonight's party.

00:04:56.320 --> 00:05:02.530
If you go out dressed like that,
he'll get bored with you and call off the engagement.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:05.670
Change into a dress.

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:06.860
Right now.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.080
But...

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:10.490
As a member of the Malvin family
that prides itself on its military tradition...

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:12.900
Not that spiel again, foolish girl!

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:13.940
Alice-chan.

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:16.630
You must understand what Elice is saying.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:21.210
You should know that we, the Malvin family, and the Schultz family are on cordial terms.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:24.550
If you wish to raise the Malvin family's reputation,

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:27.250
then consider the significance of going to the party.

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:41.770
How do I look, Sister?

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:43.390
Lovely!

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:45.370
Not bad.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:47.020
Then let us be on our way.

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:48.490
Wait.

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:59.480
For a lady who is about to meet a gentleman
to have something like that swing over her chest,

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:03.000
not even Mother wants to see such silliness happen.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.180
Then, I wish to bring something else with me...

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:08.710
...as a symbol of the Malvin family!

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:18.250
Oh, Alice!

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:21.100
Alice, beautiful Alice!

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:25.210
Please forgive me for my impatience in coming here to pick you up.

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:28.710
I am grateful for your invitation.

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:33.780
But, isn't it a bit too early to go to the party-

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:35.200
Please, accept this!

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:39.870
Although one million roses do not even come close to matching your beauty,

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:41.640
please do accept these.

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:44.550
He doesn't listen to what others are saying, as usual.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:46.890
Well then!

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:48.980
Can I have your time before the party?

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:50.360
A stroll, perhaps?

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:51.640
Why?

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:53.590
It's been such a long time since we last met.

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:55.850
Do you not want to enjoy talking with me?

00:06:56.510 --> 00:07:00.200
Fellow oneesamas, allow me to borrow your sister for a time.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:01.720
Go on, go on.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:03.200
Take her away.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:04.310
Sister!

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:22.390
Was that all right?

00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:24.300
It'll be interesting, no?

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:28.440
We are finally all alone.

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:31.320
We can finally talk about our future.

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:32.620
Future?

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.330
Yes, dearest Alice!

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:36.260
<i>Our</i>  future!

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:46.780
Supplies from Central are sent on a regular basis, eh?

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:49.060
There are even records of the feudal lord's receipt.

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:51.800
If they're not going into the hands of the civilians,

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:54.110
we only got one place to check.

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:55.240
The feudal lord.

00:07:58.260 --> 00:07:59.250
What's wrong?

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:00.640
Over there.

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:04.520
Here you go.

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:05.300
There's plenty-

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:06.750
A soup kitchen, eh?

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:10.090
There are starving people everywhere these days.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:11.630
Please line up properly.

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:14.890
It's volunteer work.

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:17.260
Some nobles do it themselves,

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:19.350
some are only civilian level.

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:22.250
That's probably run by civilians.

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:24.110
Ah, we see it now.

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:25.870
The feudal lord's castle.

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:37.580
Your dress today really matches you perfectly!

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:40.240
It makes your beauty stand out.

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:43.120
Inelegant army clothing isn't able to do that.

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:45.420
What are you trying to say?

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:47.020
You should know.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.190
You are the daughter of a noble.

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:52.940
You should be a maiden training to be a bride right now.

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:56.510
That should be your true appearance!

00:08:56.900 --> 00:08:58.640
Please quit the army!

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:02.750
The job you have at Section III doesn't reward you at all.

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:07.300
Do you hear what the commoners are calling you?

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:09.230
Let them say whatever they want.

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:11.200
They are attacking my loved one,

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:13.930
and that deeply saddens my heart.

00:09:13.930 --> 00:09:16.400
There is nothing for you to weep about, Lord Schultz.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:18.480
These are mere sentiments of the poor!

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:20.940
Why must you take on these tasks?

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:24.730
Such dirty work is not a noble's job.

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:29.630
Even now, there are people taking on
those tasks even without your presence.

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:37.800
It's useless.

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:39.380
All the doors are the same.

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:42.600
They're all shut tight,
and there's no trace that they've moved at all.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:44.680
No one responded even when I yelled.

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:46.700
No one's here, then?

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:50.900
Nah, I saw a set of fresh tire tracks over there.

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:52.440
It's only a lock, too,

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:54.170
so it'll be a piece of cake to get in.

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:56.740
That method again?

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.610
You need to know various things to feed yourself.

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:12.380
Okay!

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:19.340
Damn, this place sucks.

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:22.350
A feudal lord should keep his place a bit tidier.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:29.150
Mercury!

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:39.150
Lord Ian, we have intruders!

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:51.840
Oh, come on.

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:53.290
It's the supplies.

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:55.230
But why...

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:57.800
But damn this place stinks.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:00.910
It's kind of pointless if he keeps everything to himself but lets them rot.

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:03.720
What is the guy thinking?

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:12.370
This is weird.

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:14.900
Yeah, this reeks so much, my nose is dying.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:16.410
That's not what I meant.

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:18.670
The time between shots is way too short.

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:19.980
They're not bolt action rifles.

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:25.410
These rifles are awesome.

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.120
Semi-automatic rifles?

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:31.450
You're shitting me.

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:33.250
I only heard they were in the trial phase!

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:36.730
Besides, why does a rural feudal lord have this kind of weapon?

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:39.760
We can't even move like this.

00:11:42.460 --> 00:11:44.150
Damn it! Not again!

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:45.200
Enough.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:45.980
Stop shooting.

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:49.070
Get lost, you bandits!

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:50.750
Bandits?

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:51.930
Let's wait until nightfall.

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:53.580
We need to see what's going on.

00:11:56.970 --> 00:11:58.220
Hurry.

00:11:58.220 --> 00:11:59.570
You need to let the boss know about this.

00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:13.650
I'm starving, man.

00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:16.920
I can't believe you can say that with this stench around us.

00:12:33.490 --> 00:12:34.570
The gun backfired?!

00:12:34.570 --> 00:12:35.630
Great.

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:36.930
I'll go in.

00:12:37.300 --> 00:12:38.240
What are you going to do?!

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:41.280
You two go in and take the feudal lord into custody.

00:12:41.790 --> 00:12:43.690
Are you... going to use that?

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:45.610
Please go.

00:12:46.190 --> 00:12:46.990
Hurry!

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:52.030
I don't like the feeling of this.

00:12:52.610 --> 00:12:55.420
They can't call us the free and easygoing Section III anymore.

00:12:58.180 --> 00:12:59.380
Die, bandit!

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:03.260
Wait!

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:09.050
What's up with him?

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:19.440
Lady Alice!

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:22.250
Please seriously consider your marriage.

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:24.540
That is not only for your father's sake,

00:13:24.890 --> 00:13:27.770
but also for the sake of everyone that loves you.

00:13:27.770 --> 00:13:29.890
Yes, that is correct!

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:33.120
Your dress appearance is your true form!

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:34.620
It's a woman's happiness!

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:37.920
If you believe post-war relief is your lifetime duty,

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:42.620
aren't you able to assist the poor even as a noble?

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:47.720
I take pride in my duty at Section III.

00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:50.500
Amazing!

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:53.340
I love you more and more now.

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:55.540
Yes, that is correct!

00:13:55.540 --> 00:14:01.870
If you desire it, I will not even hesitate to give away all my money to the poor!

00:14:01.870 --> 00:14:04.040
What I truly desire is you!

00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:06.530
Without you, I wouldn't exist.

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:08.790
I surely don't need the money!

00:14:09.310 --> 00:14:10.070
Really?

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:14.410
Will you really give away all your money?

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.150
If you desire it.

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:22.780
Lord Schultz.

00:14:22.780 --> 00:14:24.510
Please distance yourself a bit.

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:29.340
Mercury!

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:32.910
What's the matter?

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:34.000
Is this a mission?

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:35.050
Lady Alice.

00:14:35.050 --> 00:14:36.260
That dog is...

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:38.030
Our section's messenger dog.

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:50.110
Sorry for stopping you.

00:14:50.830 --> 00:14:52.220
Hurry to Section III.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:56.720
Lord Schultz, I shall be borrowing your carriage.

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:22.980
What the hell is he?!

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:24.920
That flame is...

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:28.090
What is that, Lord Ian?!

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:34.710
Kill him!

00:15:34.710 --> 00:15:36.050
Hurry up and kill him!!

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:48.660
More!

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:49.890
Fire more!

00:15:56.610 --> 00:15:57.640
Corporal!

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:33.820
Hey, put your guns down.

00:16:33.820 --> 00:16:35.490
Feudal Lord Ian, correct?

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:37.080
Don't come near me!

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:38.690
Don't come near me, bandits!

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:41.320
We're not bandits, already.

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:42.640
Imperial S.S. III here!

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:52.430
Sorry for being late.

00:16:58.430 --> 00:16:59.410
Are you all right?

00:17:00.510 --> 00:17:02.100
What about you, 2nd Lieutenant?

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:04.200
What are you doing here?

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:08.230
Does a LT need a reason to be on the scene?

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:17.450
We got those rifles.

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:18.520
From who?

00:17:18.520 --> 00:17:19.720
I don't know.

00:17:20.370 --> 00:17:24.020
I don't even know if it was a man or a woman.

00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:26.240
I was just... given these.

00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:30.220
LT, if there's no manufacturer markings,

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:31.910
then there's no serial number on them either.

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:33.220
That's impossible!

00:17:33.220 --> 00:17:35.450
Then look with your own eyes.

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:47.100
I understand what you're trying to say.

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:50.030
The frenzy of bandits is a deep problem,

00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:54.960
but, that does not mean your monopolizing of the supplies can be forgiven.

00:17:55.650 --> 00:17:57.860
The civilians are what scare me the most.

00:17:58.350 --> 00:18:01.550
I'd rather have the supplies rot than give them over.

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:02.930
What?!

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:08.250
They all hate feudal lords.

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:13.270
They want revenge for being forced into an impoverished lifestyle for the victory in the war,

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:16.500
and I heard the accounts of civilians killing feudal lords are countless!

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:18.590
Right? Isn't that right?!

00:18:18.590 --> 00:18:21.990
Then the only thing I can do is protect myself, right?

00:18:22.590 --> 00:18:24.110
That surely is some hoax.

00:18:24.470 --> 00:18:26.600
Did the person that gave you the rifles tell you that?

00:18:27.900 --> 00:18:29.360
And that's why you closed yourself in your castle, eh?

00:18:29.890 --> 00:18:31.460
Where are your servants?

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:32.960
I gave them holidays.

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:38.740
The only ones left are ones that have served my family for generations and have sworn loyalty to the master.

00:18:41.190 --> 00:18:42.200
Machs.

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:44.060
Contact the nearest police station.

00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:45.180
Yes, sir.

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:48.710
Have them take custody of Lord Ian until further notice from the army.

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:54.370
To make people believe a big lie,

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:56.650
a bit of truth needs to be mixed in.

00:18:57.020 --> 00:19:01.070
The person that gave him the rifles
knows how to manipulate people's hearts.

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:03.310
You mean the civilians that killed their lords?

00:19:03.670 --> 00:19:06.860
Some incidents like that did happen right after the war ended.

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:09.430
It was in the newspapers, too.

00:19:09.430 --> 00:19:10.440
LT.

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:12.620
Now that Wolkins's tank has disappeared,

00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:15.430
those rifles are now important evidence.

00:19:15.860 --> 00:19:17.340
We need to guard them carefully.

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:20.030
You mean this is related to the tank incident?

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:21.800
I believe so.

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:29.930
By the way, LT...

00:19:30.820 --> 00:19:32.900
What about them?

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.670
Oh, shoot.

00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:38.820
I forgot.

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:40.410
Don't tell me...

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:43.880
...that's the LT's fiancé?

00:19:43.880 --> 00:19:44.940
Him?!

00:19:45.510 --> 00:19:47.110
What do you think, man?

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:48.560
What do you mean?

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:49.080
I don't know.

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:04.800
I have come to pick you up, my princess.

00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:09.930
Lord Leonir...

00:20:11.070 --> 00:20:12.160
And who is this?

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:13.640
Don't ask me.

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:16.050
The party is about to begin.

00:20:16.050 --> 00:20:17.080
Let us hurry.

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:19.580
Why are you here?

00:20:19.980 --> 00:20:22.570
I go where you go.

00:20:22.940 --> 00:20:24.720
Can it not be as such?

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:33.960
LT, we don't get what's going on.

00:20:35.070 --> 00:20:38.710
This is my fiancé, Leonir Taylor.

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:39.880
Huh?

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:40.460
Eh?

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:43.720
Y-You're Lady Alice's fiancé?!

00:20:46.840 --> 00:20:49.600
You seem to be done with your work here.

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:50.740
Shall we?

00:20:56.550 --> 00:20:58.360
What are you hesitating for?

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:02.170
I am proud of how you look when you fight.

00:21:08.170 --> 00:21:09.560
Well then, Schultz.

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:11.230
See you later at the party.

00:21:11.860 --> 00:21:13.620
Make sure you're not late, eh?

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:17.100
I-I won't lose to you, Leonir!

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:21.600
Lady Alice is still swaying between you and I!

00:21:21.600 --> 00:21:23.730
Sure didn't seem so...

00:21:23.730 --> 00:21:26.130
So, who are you exactly?

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:30.950
A job well done.

00:21:31.480 --> 00:21:34.550
I hope the standard of living changes for the civilians after this.

00:21:35.720 --> 00:21:39.110
It's as if you knew about everything.

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:40.680
But, of course,

00:21:41.290 --> 00:21:45.020
for I was the one who gave the tip to Section III.

00:21:46.430 --> 00:21:51.310
I share the same outrage against this era as you, my princess.

00:23:30.510 --> 00:23:33.930
Mer-kun, our mission next time is to deliver something through a snowy mountain.

00:23:33.930 --> 00:23:37.450
Everyone, please be careful against raids by mountain bandits!

00:23:37.450 --> 00:23:40.210
Oh no, they're here already after I just mentioned them!

00:23:40.210 --> 00:23:42.300
Next time, "Burning in the the Fields of Snow".

00:23:42.300 --> 00:23:44.360
Come get us if you're not scared!
